<CapaProblem id="uk_kg_palace" title="Kensington Gardens: history" dontKnow="true">
  <KeyGrader>
    <Markdown>Who created the private gardens of Kensington Palace in 1689?</Markdown>
    <ChoiceInput>
      <Distractor>Queen Victoria</Distractor>
      <Key>William III and Mary II (carved from Hyde Park)</Key>
      <Distractor>Henry VIII</Distractor>
    </ChoiceInput>
    <Explanation>
      <Markdown>In 1689 William III and Mary II bought Nottingham House and carved part of Hyde Park to create a private garden for their new Kensington Palace; Christopher Wren enlarged the house. Mary had Dutch-style flower beds and box hedges laid out.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>Wikipedia (Kensington Palace): the house began as a Jacobean mansion of 1605; George II died there in 1760, the last reigning monarch to live there; Queen Victoria was born there on 24 May 1819.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>*Source: https://www.royalparks.org.uk/visit/parks/kensington-gardens/history (confidence: high)*</Markdown>
    </Explanation>
  </KeyGrader>
