<CapaProblem id="uk_kg_caroline" title="Kensington Gardens: history" dontKnow="true">
  <KeyGrader>
    <Markdown>What is the Long Water?</Markdown>
    <ChoiceInput>
      <Distractor>A canal beside Kensington Palace</Distractor>
      <Key>The part of the Serpentine that lies inside Kensington Gardens</Key>
      <Distractor>A stream flowing into the Round Pond</Distractor>
    </ChoiceInput>
    <Explanation>
      <Markdown>In 1728 Queen Caroline and Charles Bridgeman reshaped the gardens, creating the winding Serpentine and using a ha-ha ditch rather than a fence to divide them from Hyde Park. The Serpentine's section within Kensington Gardens is the Long Water, with the Italian Gardens at its northwest head.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>Date of the Serpentine and the split vary (see Hyde Park). Italian Gardens were commissioned by Queen Victoria (Royal Parks page).</Markdown>
      <Markdown>*Source: https://www.royalparks.org.uk/visit/parks/kensington-gardens/history (confidence: medium)*</Markdown>
    </Explanation>
  </KeyGrader>
</CapaProblem>

<CapaProblem id="uk_kg_round_pond" title="Kensington Gardens: history" dontKnow="true">
  <KeyGrader>
    <Markdown>Why is the name Round Pond misleading?</Markdown>
    <ChoiceInput>
      <Distractor>It is not a pond but a river</Distractor>
      <Key>It is not round: it is roughly rectangular with rounded corners</Key>
      <Distractor>It is in Hyde Park, not Kensington Gardens</Distractor>
    </ChoiceInput>
    <Explanation>
      <Markdown>The Round Pond, in front of Kensington Palace, was created in 1730 under George II, is about seven acres and 5 metres deep at most, and is not round but rectangular with rounded corners. It is a centre of model yacht sailing.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>Wikipedia only; many sources say 1728 for the Caroline works. The Royal Parks page does not mention the Round Pond. Model Yacht Sailing Association founded 1876.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>*Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Round_Pond_(London) (confidence: medium)*</Markdown>
    </Explanation>
  </KeyGrader>
</CapaProblem>

<CapaProblem id="uk_albert_what" title="Kensington Gardens: Albert Memorial" dontKnow="true">
