      <Distractor>Sir Jacob Epstein; Queen Victoria</Distractor>
    </ChoiceInput>
    <Explanation>
      <Markdown>The bronze Peter Pan statue is by Sir George Frampton, commissioned and paid for by J. M. Barrie. It stands west of the Long Water, near Barrie's former home on Bayswater Road, where Peter lands in The Little White Bird.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>The Royal Parks page says Barrie paid for a bronze statue in 1912. The Little White Bird (1902) is the book in which Peter first appeared.</Markdown>
