<CapaProblem id="uk_pol_so_hostage_mp" title="The State Opening of Parliament" dontKnow="true">
  <KeyGrader>
    <Markdown>Why is an MP kept at Buckingham Palace during the State Opening?</Markdown>
    <ChoiceInput>
      <Key>As a ceremonial hostage, a surety for the Sovereign's safe return from Parliament</Key>
      <Distractor>To announce the King's arrival to the Commons</Distractor>
      <Distractor>To guard the Imperial State Crown</Distractor>
      <Distractor>To carry the Speech to Parliament</Distractor>
    </ChoiceInput>
    <Explanation>
      <Markdown>An MP, usually the Vice-Chamberlain of the Household, is held at Buckingham Palace as a ceremonial hostage to guarantee the Sovereign's safe return.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>parliament.uk traces the custom to Charles I's quarrel with Parliament. The Vice-Chamberlain is a member of the Royal Household and a junior Government whip.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>*Source: https://www.parliament.uk/about/living-heritage/evolutionofparliament/parliamentwork/offices-and-ceremonies/overview/state-opening/elements-unseen-by-the-public/ (confidence: high)*</Markdown>
    </Explanation>
  </KeyGrader>
</CapaProblem>

<CapaProblem id="uk_pol_so_standard" title="The State Opening of Parliament" dontKnow="true">
