<CapaProblem id="uk_pol_so_door" title="The State Opening of Parliament" dontKnow="true">
  <KeyGrader>
    <Markdown>What happens when Black Rod reaches the door of the House of Commons?</Markdown>
    <ChoiceInput>
      <Distractor>The Mace is lowered across the door</Distractor>
      <Distractor>The door is opened by the Speaker at once</Distractor>
      <Key>The door is slammed in Black Rod's face; Black Rod strikes it three times with the staff and is then admitted</Key>
      <Distractor>Black Rod rings a bell twice</Distractor>
    </ChoiceInput>
    <Explanation>
      <Markdown>Black Rod is sent to summon the Commons. The Commons door is shut in Black Rod's face to show the Commons' independence from the monarchy. Black Rod strikes it three times with the rod and is then admitted.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>parliament.uk dates the custom to the Civil War; its Living Heritage Black Rod page cites a 1641 Commons Journal entry, and the public-sequence page links it to Charles I's 1642 attempt to arrest five MPs.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>*Source: https://www.parliament.uk/about/how/occasions/stateopening/ (confidence: high)*</Markdown>
    </Explanation>
  </KeyGrader>
</CapaProblem>

<CapaProblem id="uk_pol_so_commons_walk" title="The State Opening of Parliament" dontKnow="true">
