<CapaProblem id="uk_pol_tory" title="The two major parties" dontKnow="true">
  <KeyGrader>
    <Markdown>Where does the nickname "Tory" come from?</Markdown>
    <ChoiceInput>
      <Key>An insult from the 1678-81 Exclusion crisis, from an Irish word for outlaw or robber</Key>
      <Distractor>A Roman word for ruler</Distractor>
      <Distractor>The name of Peel's constituency</Distractor>
      <Distractor>A Scottish word for landowner</Distractor>
    </ChoiceInput>
    <Explanation>
      <Markdown>The word Tory began as an insult in the Exclusion Bill crisis of 1678 to 1681, from an Irish word for an outlaw or robber.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>*Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conservative_Party_(UK) (confidence: medium)*</Markdown>
    </Explanation>
  </KeyGrader>
</CapaProblem>

