<CapaProblem id="uk_pol_dev_referendums" title="Devolution" dontKnow="true">
  <KeyGrader>
    <Markdown>When did Scotland and Wales vote for devolution?</Markdown>
    <ChoiceInput>
      <Distractor>1999</Distractor>
      <Distractor>1979</Distractor>
      <Key>In referendums in September 1997</Key>
      <Distractor>2014</Distractor>
    </ChoiceInput>
    <Explanation>
      <Markdown>Devolution followed referendums: Scotland and Wales voted in September 1997, Northern Ireland approved the Good Friday Agreement in May 1998.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>Wales voted yes by only 6,721 votes (senedd.wales); a Welsh referendum on St David's Day 1979 had rejected devolution nearly 4 to 1.</Markdown>
      <Markdown>*Source: https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/devolution-guidance-for-civil-servants/devolution-guidance-for-civil-servants (confidence: high)*</Markdown>
    </Explanation>
  </KeyGrader>
</CapaProblem>

